me greenhouse  elements I really love greenhouses in  botanical gardens and such where you can  step into a tropical or desert biome and  this building is very similar to that  generally it was a way to put a bunch of  palm trees in the middle of this and  then mix it with some exhibits  I only fit for exhibits into this  building because they're really  expensive which I didn't really realize  before I built this but it makes sense  totally but it meant that I couldn't  really go all out on this building  unless I not run out of money which in  fact I did  at the end of construction of this one  so I have to stop adding stuff to it at  some point but yeah that's basically it  so this is what it looks like from the  outside with the glass arches and the  towers and I think it's a decent mix of  the two materials at least I'm pretty  happy with it  now moving into a much smaller blueprint  this is going to be a small store for  food which I figured was also quite  necessary so far all the blueprints have  been very large and fairly expensive so  I wanted to build something small that  you could actually just lop down next to  a road and turn into a snack corner or  something like that and for this one I'm  again bringing back the sandstone pieces  to use a few more sensitive pieces that  I haven't used before I'm actually using  a domed pavilion for the site there and  then putting some tower pieces on top of  that which I think works fairly well and  then there are a bunch of different  decorations and trims on top of the  walls this building will be much simpler  than some of the other ones it's really  just coming down to you know if you have  a very simple shape a very simple  building which is just a food store how  can you add detail to it what are the  scenery pieces like and it's especially  a good building for stuff like clutter  so you can see me browsing a lot through  the clutter section here and I have to  say it's absolutely amazing I think the  Indian theme is probably my favorite in  the game so far for all of the clutter  options alone lots of baskets and sex  and even fruits and all kinds of things  that you would need to build a  marketplace but these can really be used  quite well to add the scenery of areas I  put a little rickshaw under the roof as  well I don't know maybe in the plots of  this building it could be used as some  sort of delivery service but you know  given that I wanted to add a small roof  to this building to make it a little bit  less Square and boxy putting a rickshaw  underneath it would be quite realistic I  guess so  that's it for this building this is what  this blueprint looks like in the end and  with that said it's time to move on to  the final blueprints of this this whole  video which is going to be a toilets  building because I didn't have any  toilets so far and I've always forgotten  about toilets beard in my Park Tech  videos or planet coaster videos or  rollercoaster kin 3 videos or even  roller coaster [ __ ] videos I just always  forget about toilets and  in this case I'm gonna try to change my  ways and become a better person and not  forget about toilets anymore and my  first step is to build an Indian toilet  blueprints before I forget that actually  come to think of it my first blueprint  in this game was a toilet the the tudor  toilets but yeah anyway this is going to  be a very simple building as well not  much bigger than a toilet building would  realistically need to be but I'm  experimenting with a few different  pieces in this one mostly the limestone  pieces to see how they work together  with the other wall pieces I should say  I'm using a lot of painted walls here  because from my quote-unquote research  of google imaging a lot of Indian cities  in architecture I found that painted  walls seems to be quite a common thing  so I ended up using painted walls on all  of these blueprints in some way and on  this one I tried combining them with the  limestone pieces to see how that works  together and there's even some brick as  an extra detail to add some color into  this building  lest it not be completely white and very  monochrome so I think these textures  honestly work very well together and it  might just be because you know the game  is quite new and we haven't seen a lot  of pieces being used I think in planet  coaster for instance the fact that the  game is a few years old does make it a  bit more boring to see the same pieces  over and over again and everything here  is still fresh so that automatically  kind of makes things look more  interesting I think but still a lot of  these different textures from even the  different themes in the game work really  well together I think given the fact  that the limestone pieces come from the  classic theme the painted walls are a  generic thing I think and then the other  details are all from the Indian theme  but even so they all fit very well  together I think so I'm really happy  about that  although to actually make these  buildings look sufficiently Indian I'm  really focusing on the Indian theme when  it comes to the minor details like the  windows and arches and brackets and  things like that  I was actually considering for a while  to put some sort of dome or decoration  on top of the front of this building but  I've done that for every building in  this bank so  and I really wanted one building which  is a bit more subdued and simple  not to mention that domes are pretty  expensive you know not in the game but  realistically speaking so I needed to  calm it down a little bit on my dome  fixation so ended up not including one  in this build also this was my first  time messing around with the vines in  the game and they're absolutely amazing  there's such an improvement over the  planet coaster one and it's it's a nice  small touch to any building I think to  make it look a bit more lift in and a  bit more like an actual old building and  yeah that is basically it for this  blueprint I put some foliage around it  to make it look a bit more like it's  actually in an Indian context but that's  about it so yeah I'd like to thank you  guys for watching this video and  hopefully I'll see you in a planet to  franchise video sometime soon and if you  want to check out any of the blueprints  just a reminder that they'll be down in  the description there will be a link to  the workshop bye guys
 

